From: pocknix <pocknix@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: vtdr6130-rp6: fix swapped frame-rate select values

Measured on hardware: with the init sequence writing 0x6C 0x00 (the
driver's "120Hz" value) the panel's TE pulses at 60/s against 120Hz DPU
timings, so alternate command-mode kickoffs miss TE and time out
(21 err/s steady, effective ~60fps output; with the pre-1021 mode-guess
race this mismatch could also half-lock tearcheck into a TE-dead state,
~10fps). The rare fully-good sessions were the race accidentally taking
the "60Hz" branch, i.e. 0x6C 0x01 is the real 120Hz select. Swap them.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-visionox-vtdr6130-cog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-visionox-vtdr6130-cog.c
@@ -103,11 +103,17 @@
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x36, 0x02);
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x59, 0x09);
 
+	/*
+	 * Frame-rate select: 0x01 = 120Hz, 0x00 = 60Hz. The original driver had
+	 * these swapped; with 0x00 the panel measurably runs 60Hz internal
+	 * refresh (TE at 60/s) against 120Hz DPU timings, so half the
+	 * command-mode kickoffs miss TE and time out.
+	 */
 	if (cur_vrefresh == 120) {
-		mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x6C, 0x00);
+		mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x6C, 0x01);
 	}
 	else {
-		mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x6C, 0x01);
+		mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x6C, 0x00);
 	}
 
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0x6D, 0x00);
